{"title":"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 9c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Official_Solution,_Proof_by_Contradiction)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Official Solution, Proof by Contradiction)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a1fbb8951975f2af152b5c26c760e5adc0cfdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a,b) = \\dfrac{a}{b} + \\dfrac{b}{a} + \\dfrac{1}{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"170\" height=\"39\" />. For example, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eedb031d99fdbc698f81eeb1dd3a9c5806f18e90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_9c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/07254b24b1c3168cfbf6984fa9fc22b1aa0fb6df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> is an integer, prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/07254b24b1c3168cfbf6984fa9fc22b1aa0fb6df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> must be a multiple of 3.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Official_Solution.2C_Proof_by_Contradiction.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Official_Solution,_Proof_by_Contradiction)\">Solution 1 (Official Solution, Proof by Contradiction)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_9c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Official Solution, Proof by Contradiction)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can do a proof of contradiction, assuming that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189a3f8380b67b3632c243ee7c4f31e40e485a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> is <i>not</i> a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/6/596af81f452d66ec2a2538ca8bdbc6671fd410ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a, b) = \\frac{a}{b} + \\frac{b}{a} + \\frac{1}{ab} = \\frac{a \\times a}{b \\times a} + \\frac{b \\times b}{a \\times b} + \\frac{1}{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"349\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb195a2bfadf85fe10234b3e1206c5e42f30f7f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{a^{2}}{ab} + \\frac{b^{2}}{ab} + \\frac{1}{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/0512fda53812649a6b8aa83eb6f06ed7695c19ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{a^{2} + b^{2} + 1}{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ad13158a058cae9b585abc3dc120d4ec4a891f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = f(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />, we then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/90770d9708785566879266e6b6a238785a858a45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{a^{2} + b^{2} + 1}{ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"127\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15adf51273b56a84c6493534798508ccf7e281e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abn = a^{2} + b^{2} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26c867b123887ef9a1b69a8d17d03558ee9ff93d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} - abn + b^{2} + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f6b1822921ff6ebfc73c2ca2428601d76a147f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} - (bn)a + (b^{2} + 1) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"200\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We then realize that we can use the quadratic formula with this, using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> as the variable:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b3c44b1dbff2aabd90f926ed3d4336e629254e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{-(-bn) \\pm \\sqrt{(bn)^{2} - 4 \\times 1 \\times (b^{2} + 1)}}{2 \\times 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"327\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b26d72c8d870a80e774a18598b1eb2f2c6cf426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{bn \\pm \\sqrt{b^{2}n^{2} - 4 \\times b^{2} - 4 \\times 1}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"261\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee533bc3ae9b1b296ed58230c464e29f023db91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\frac{bn \\pm \\sqrt{b^{2}n^{2} - 4b^{2} - 4}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f92a4b3e00079f843a4a4212f35c2143ff82657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2}n^{2} - 4b^{2} - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> must be a perfect square because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer. We have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38f2b0cbb10abea8fe7768ae05e31e1f497a5deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2}n^{2} - 4b^{2} - 4 = b^{2}(n^{2} - 4) - 4 = b^{2}(n - 2)(n + 2) - 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"431\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it must either be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In the first case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> must also be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In the second case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/438ca8cfe4ef1f8af9be1b9ba6670a87cced8f11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/5418d99e27f886bdabf0976f3f3eb26d189d7dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2}(n - 2)(n + 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in either case, so we can represent it as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/990be3a6569dcb460d9b32a5dd65ef7046a51cad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} \\times 3m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer. We then have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/5393b31a3d8c4b4bdafef61da26e09f167ced135.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} \\times 3m - 4 = 3b^{2}m - 6 + 2 = 3(b^{2}m - 2) + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"364\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904d75b99def97c2e5e9148d837d5d5db5e8b3ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(b^{2}m - 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we realize that the discriminant must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>However, we realize that this cannot be possible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7138e1c6949cd5065e80fbd7726db4b2dc4d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4f3ae887ebc147cf15b2ed474a142220ede61d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, which has a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we realize that if the discrimant is a perfect square but is not a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, it must have a remainder of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Our remainder is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we have reached a contradiction.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ad13158a058cae9b585abc3dc120d4ec4a891f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = f(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher and CEMC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_9c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can follow the same steps as solution 1 to the point where we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15adf51273b56a84c6493534798508ccf7e281e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abn = a^{2} + b^{2} + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ad13158a058cae9b585abc3dc120d4ec4a891f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = f(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We can split this problem into two cases: one where either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and another where neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If a number is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then its square must have the same remainder as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/018827d417ec36f614b2a42685027d2430389e21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^{2} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If a number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then its square must have the same remainder as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7138e1c6949cd5065e80fbd7726db4b2dc4d3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If a number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then its square must have the same remainder as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4f3ae887ebc147cf15b2ed474a142220ede61d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which has the same remainder as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modular_arithmetic\" title=\"Modular arithmetic\">modular arithmetic</a> for the first case, this means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3e2b6f26fae080d25755d4d4a0d8572c5e43094.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0bn \\equiv 0 + b^{2} + 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d53fbb12c0e2b89880a2240bb1b72ea107946fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} + 1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a1583c4b9f5623f6491d345ab85030cc44b3a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^{2} \\equiv -1 \\pmod {3} \\equiv 2 \\pmod {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"242\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>However, as we saw above, there is no way for the remainder to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, so this case is not possible. Similarly, we cannot have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3caf2c7750e40945bc5090573ec6fd19274605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a, b) = f(b, a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />, meaning that we get the same exact result but flipped for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Next, for the second case, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/8/e38774e8bd863fa66af13d8d259b5dda7ff1e101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{2} + b^{2} + 1 \\equiv 1 + 1 + 1 \\pmod {3} \\equiv 3 \\pmod {3} \\equiv 0 \\pmod {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"467\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c741677b3251ae2c310a49d935a109a8d1ac28c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abn \\equiv a^{2} + b^{2} + 1 \\pmod {3} \\equiv 0 \\pmod {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"318\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14b78d0b7b2414e605ba9d482916bcd6c5f8de7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are <i>not</i> divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8ad13158a058cae9b585abc3dc120d4ec4a891f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = f(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011028\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 396/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17417/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.958      1 2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_9\n100.00%    6.958      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36005:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018011028 and revision id 279856. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}